# 41. Preliminary Operationalization

The Safe & Sane framework has been explored through preliminary controlled interaction with an AI system identified as Ox Alpha.

The appropriate interpretation is limited.

Such testing does not establish:

- scientific proof;
- universal validity;
- generalization across AI systems;
- superiority over existing safety frameworks;
- causal effectiveness;
- complete safety.

If testing demonstrates that a DOS can be instantiated operationally and that configuration-oriented constraints can influence AI behaviour, the result is more appropriately described as:

Conceptual abstraction
→ Operational representation
→ AI interaction
→ Observed behaviour

This establishes an empirical basis for further experimentation.

It does not establish the framework as scientifically validated.

